    "review": {
      "verdict": "approve",
      "rationale": "The three supplied Go sources implement the step's obligations: /health/live returns 200 with the required fields; /health/ready returns 200 on success or 503 JSON with status not_ready on failure; non-GET methods return 405 JSON; unknown routes return 404 JSON; NewConfig requires DATABASE_URL. The readiness handler uses a 5s bounded context, and the server WriteTimeout is 10s, leaving handler room to return 503 JSON. TestReadinessDeadlineReturnsJSON uses the actual production http.Server (not httptest defaults), an atomic call counter, an invalidDeadline flag, and cleanup/join via closeDeadlineTestServer. The shutdown-v13 patch adds shutdownDone synchronization so main waits for Shutdown to finish after ListenAndServe returns ErrServerClosed, with forced Close on shutdown error, matching the installed Server.Shutdown documentation. The main startup DB context is 10s and separated from the long-lived signal.Background context; SIGINT and SIGTERM are registered via signal.NotifyContext; a fresh bounded shutdown context is used; raw DB errors are not logged. Test evidence shows 7 tests pass, vet/build exit 0, and the deadline regression was RED at 5s (EOF) and GREEN at 10s. The later headless operator probe demonstrates a real dedicated PostgreSQL identity with actual pgxpool.Ping/acquisition via source handlers, with no credential leaks and no actual main-process success claim. All constraints are respected: the prototype is not promoted, actual app sources are absent, and no autonomous repair/learning success is claimed.",
